            <ArticleTitle>Crystal structure of (Z)-N-benzyl-idene-1-phenyl-methanamine oxide hydrogen peroxide monosolvate.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1666-1669</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1107/S2056989017014499</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The title adduct, C14H13NO·H2O2, consists of (Z)-N-benzyl-idene-1-phenyl-methanamine oxide and hydrogen peroxide mol-ecules in a 1:1 ratio. The organic coformer adopts a skew geometry with an inter-aryl-ring dihedral angle of 81.9 (2)°. In the crystal, the organic and peroxide mol-ecules are linked through both peroxide O-H donor groups to oxide O-atom acceptors, giving one-dimensional chains extending along the b axis. Present also are weak inter-molecular C-H⋯O hydrogen-bonding inter-actions.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
